From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ned <github@edoardo.fyi>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 15:54:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 43/90] Yield pure guest polls at scheduler and IOP deadlines

Expose the IOP scheduler's existing idle bound in EE cycles, including SPU2
service/event deadlines, fractional cycle carry and synchronous RPC credit.
Invalidate the bound when the final SPU2 advance raises an interrupt.

Reuse waitForEvent for a wall-clock-only idlePoll primitive. Anchor relative
deadlines before IOP service, account elapsed host time before and after the
wait, and return to the dispatcher for interrupts/callbacks. Runnable EE work
and deterministic-cycle timing keep the original poll path.

Integrated Tarzan swap-poll A/B, task user+system CPU in steady gameplay:
mission 1 at 25 FPS: 1.351457 -> 0.806470 CPU s/s (-40.33%),
54.058 -> 32.259 ms/frame; at 60 FPS: 1.515577 -> 1.124713 CPU s/s
(-25.79%), 25.260 -> 18.745 ms/frame. Both pairs hold 25.0/60.0 FPS,
zero steady underruns and zero VU fallbacks. Control/candidate run back to
back with TARZAN_SWAP_IDLE=0/1; no tracing or verification during timing.

Validation: tz build; tz test; tz test --full (56/56 ctest,
1130 VU replay runs, zero mismatches/rejected/skipped); mission 1 default,
60 FPS A/B, verify mode; mission 8 at 60 FPS; full first-mission movie/audio
route (25.0 FPS, zero steady underruns/fallbacks, no crash).

